Assume that you have an InputStream whose next bytes are XYZABC. What is the result of calling the following method on the stream, using a count value of 3?
<pre>
public static String pullBytes(InputStream is, int count) throws IOException {
  is.mark(count);
  final StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
  for(int i=0; i&lt;count; i++)
    sb.append((char)is.read());
  is.reset();
  is.skip(1);
  sb.append((char)is.read());
  return sb.toString();
}
</pre>
